{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8xOTk5LS1CZWZvcmUvRWlnaHQlMjBNZW4lMjBPdXQlMjAlMjgxOTg4JTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Eight Men Out","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/9nh0w2C9h9KfJb0OsVg65O65b5s.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6v594uUI5VOBjdlxiV0d6EOjvW.jpg","description":"Buck Weaver and Hap Felsch are young idealistic players on the Chicago White Sox, a pennant-winning team owned by Charles Comiskey -  a penny-pinching, hands-on manager who underpays his players and treats them with disdain. And when gamblers and hustlers discover that Comiskey's demoralized players are ripe for a money-making scheme, one by one the team members agree to throw the World Series. But when the White Sox are defeated, a couple of sports writers smell a fix and a national scandal explodes, ripping the cover off America's favorite pastime.","releaseInfo":"1988","genres":["Drama","History","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.8","runtime":"120 min","cast":["John Cusack","Clifton James","Michael Lerner","Christopher Lloyd","John Mahoney","Charlie Sheen","David Strathairn","D. B. Sweeney"],"director":["John Sayles"],"released":"1988-09-02T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"When the cheering stopped, there were... Eight Men Out.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"John Cusack","character":"Buck Weaver","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/aCwCx6JU7Jxbg6Q1ygcnLY750le.jpg"},{"name":"Clifton James","character":"Charles Comiskey","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/4XRoVhgoeQEZdg4BAKCWRkI1UfR.jpg"},{"name":"Michael Lerner","character":"Arnold Rothstein","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/1jRm6TRS5atQrA1VQSef7GoL13g.jpg"},{"name":"Christopher Lloyd","character":"Bill Burns","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/nxVjpyb3UrfbPZnEyDNlQVlFAs5.jpg"},{"name":"John Mahoney","character":"Kid Gleason","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/paVSw7Brdp6MKa2j4UPukA0KHs3.jpg"},{"name":"Charlie Sheen","character":"Hap Felsch","photo":"htt